dracopedia.title.start=§l§6Dragon Mounts Guide
dracopedia.body.start=§r§fWelcome to Dragon Mounts!\nDragon Mounts 2 is proudly brought to you by the Official DragonMountsTeam.\n\nAs you explore the world, you’ll discover unique structures that contain dragon eggs.\n\nVisit the How To Play section to learn how to hatch, raise, and ride your dragons!
dracopedia.button.how_to_play=How to Play
dracopedia.button.credits=Credits
dracopedia.button.dragons=Dragons
dracopedia.title.how_to_play=How to Play
dracopedia.body.how_to_play=Before you begin your journey, choose the type of guidance you need.
dracopedia.button.back=Back
dracopedia.button.dragon_raising=Dragon Raising
dracopedia.button.egg_conversion=Egg Conversion

dracopedia.title.dragon_raising=§6§lRaising Your Dragon
dracopedia.body.dragon_raising=§fRaising your dragon involves progressing it through five growth stages.\n\n§6§lEgg Stage§r\n§fWhen you collect your first Dragon Egg, place it on the ground and right-click to begin incubation. Once activated, the egg enters a 20-minute real-time incubation period before it hatches.\n\n§6§lSpeeding Up Hatching§r\n§fYou can reduce the incubation time by using Emeralds:\n§f• Each Emerald removes a portion of the remaining time.\n§f• Using multiple Emeralds can skip the entire incubation instantly.\n\n§6§lHatchling Stage§r\n§fAs soon as the egg finishes incubating, it hatches into a Hatchling. This early stage is short but important — the dragon is small and fragile. Feed the hatchling any raw meat except pufferfish. Regular feeding will help it progress into the Juvenile stage more quickly.\n\n§6§lJuvenile Stage§r\n§fThe Juvenile stage is not a major milestone, as the dragon can do everything a Hatchling can but with increased health. Continue feeding it any type of meat to help it progress into the Adolescence stage.\n\n§6§lAdolescence Stage§r\n§fDuring Adolescence, your dragon becomes rideable, can equip armor, and gains the ability to breathe fire. Continue feeding it raw meat to help it reach the Adult stage.\n\n§6§lAdult Stage§r\n§fThe Adult stage is the dragon’s fully matured form. Adult dragons can do everything they could during Adolescence, but also gain the ability to breed with another adult dragon of the same type.

dracopedia.title.egg_conversion=Egg Conversion
dracopedia.body.egg_conversion=Each Dragon Egg can transform into another type when placed on specific blocks or exposed to certain conditions.\n\nAll conversions take §l5 real minutes§r unless lightning is involved (lightning conversions are instant).\n\n§6Aether Egg§r\n1. Place any egg on a 3×3 Glowstone platform.\n2. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Fire Egg§r\n1. Place any egg in open space.\n2. Surround the egg with Lava on all 4 sides.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Water Egg§r\n1. Place any egg in a small area.\n2. Surround it completely with Water source blocks.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Terra Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 platform using Sand or Red Sand.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Forest Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 Oak Wood or Oak Leaves platform.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Ice Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 platform from Ice, Packed Ice, Blue Ice, or Snow Blocks.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Zombie Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 platform of Mossy Cobblestone or Soul Sand.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Skeleton Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 Bone Block platform.\n2. Place a Zombie Egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Nether Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 Magma Block platform.\n2. Place any egg on top.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Ender Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 End Stone platform.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Sunlight Egg§r\n1. Place any egg on a Daylight Sensor set to Day Mode (yellow).\n2. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Moonlight Egg§r\n1. Place any egg on a Daylight Sensor set to Night Mode (blue).\n2. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Sculk Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 Sculk Block or Sculk Catalyst platform.\n2. Place the egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.\n\n§6Storm Egg§r\n1. Start with a Water Egg.\n2. Strike it with lightning (natural or Channeling).\n3. Conversion is instant.\n\n§6Wither Egg§r\n1. Start with a Skeleton Egg.\n2. Strike with lightning.\n3. Conversion is instant.\n\n§6Dark Egg§r\n1. Start with a Moonlight Egg.\n2. Strike with lightning.\n3. Conversion is instant.\n\n§6Enchanted Egg§r\n1. Build a 3×3 Bookshelf platform.\n2. Place an Ender Egg in the center.\n3. Wait 5 minutes.

dracopedia.title.how_to_use_items=§6§lHow To Use Items
dracopedia.body.how_to_use_items=§fThis page explains how to properly use key items that interact with your dragons.\n\n§6§lFlute§r\n§fThe Flute is used to command a specific dragon. To bind a flute to a dragon, §lsneak§r and interact with the dragon while holding the flute. Once bound, the flute will only control that dragon.\n\nAfter binding, the flute provides two commands:\n§f• Follow / Wander — Toggles whether the dragon roams or stays near you.\n§f• Come To Player — Calls the dragon directly to your location.\n\n§6Note:§r\n§fIf you release a dragon from an amulet, you must rebind the flute to that dragon.\n\n§6§lAmulet§r\n§fThe Amulet allows you to safely store your dragon. To use it, §lcrouch§r and hit your dragon while holding the amulet. The dragon will be safely stored without taking any damage.\n\nThe amulet will display important information about the stored dragon:\n§f• Breed\n§f• Owner\n§f• Health\n\n§6§lEssence§r\n§fWhen your dragon dies, it drops its Essence. This item is required to revive your dragon.\n\nA Dragoncore block also appears at the death location. Interact with the Dragoncore, or use the Essence on the ground, to resurrect your dragon as a baby.\n\nThe revived dragon returns with the §fsame name and variant§r it had before death.
